    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1. Number of evidence-based improvements and/or new concepts of existing SME support schemes (including targeting access to finance and diaspora financial engagement in development) developed in partnership with the Ministry of Economy and the Economic Advisory Council to the Prime Minister

1.2. Number of evidence-based policy/regulatory amendments in the field of SME development and informal employment developed in a participatory manner in partnership with the Ministry of Economy and Ministry of Labour and Social Protection

2.1. Number of LPA, private sector and community organizers capacitated in the field of entrepreneurship and investment promotion (opportunity spotting, planning, organizing the effort and evaluation)

2.2. Number of beneficiaries of peer-to-peer learning and experience exchange events

3.1. Number of value chains defined, assessed and selected for upgrade support

3.2. Number of private companies (e.g. MSME) with increased competitiveness (e.g. reduction of production costs, increase of sales volume, access to new markets, development of new products, etc.)

3.3. Number of business competitiveness improvements, resulting from the implementation of digital transformation solutions (embedded in the selected micro-clusters)

4.1. Number of public-private partnerships (PPPs) established for joint investment promotion within the selected micro-clusters and supported

4.2. Number of business partnerships established within and among the selected micro-clusters

4.3. Number of micro-cluster investment portfolios developed

5.1. Number of people (particularly of women, returning migrants and refugees, NEET from target communities) employed in the selected value chains/ cluster through the pilot intervention

5.2. Number of returning migrants from the target communities who received a comprehensive project support for a sustainable reintegration, based on the National Program

